00:59:26,666 --> 00:59:32,666
Firebird is a 2021 romantic war drama film directed, co-written, and co-produced by Peeter Rebane (in
his feature directorial debut), based on Sergey Fetisov's memoir The Story of Roman.

11
01:05:23,333 --> 01:05:29,333
The film stars Tom Prior (who also co-wrote and
co-produced), Oleg Zagorodnii, and Diana Pozharskaya.

12
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:26,000
Set in the Soviet Air Force during the Cold War, it tells the true story
of forbidden love between a private and a fighter pilot.

13
01:17:16,666 --> 01:17:22,666
Firebird had its world premiere at the 35th BFI Flare:
London LGBTIQ+ Film Festival on 17 March 2021.

14
01:23:13,333 --> 01:23:19,333
The film also screened at the 45th Frameline: San Francisco International LGBTQ+ Film
Festival on 27 June 2021, where it won an honorable mention for Best First Feature.

15
01:29:10,000 --> 01:29:16,000
The film had a limited theatrical release in the United
States by Roadside Attractions on 29 April 2022.

16
01:35:06,666 --> 01:35:12,666
The film explores themes of cold war, 1970s, lgbt,
lgbt in the military, gay theme.

17
01:41:03,333 --> 01:41:09,333
The tone is emotional.
